("Neither the lead researcher nor the laboratory assistants WERE aware of the) Tj
T*
(contamination.") Tj
T*
("Neither the laboratory assistants nor the lead researcher WAS aware of the) Tj
T*
(contamination.") Tj
T*
(* Rule 4 \(Indefinite Pronouns\): Each, every, either, neither, someone, everybody,) Tj
T*
(anyone are strictly SINGULAR:) Tj
T*
("Everybody in the department HAS submitted the annual report.") Tj
T*
(* Rule 5 \(Collective Nouns\): Singular when acting as a unified collective unit;) Tj
T*
(plural when individual members act separately:) Tj
T*
("The committee HAS reached a consensus" \(Unified\).) Tj
T*
("The committee WERE divided in their opinions" \(Individual discord\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
/F2 9.5 Tf
(>> 2.3 Question Tags in Scientific Dialogue) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(A question tag is a mini-question appended to the end of a declarative statement to seek) Tj
T*
(confirmation.) Tj
T*
(* Fundamental Rules:) Tj
T*
(1. Polarity Reversal: Positive statement takes a Negative tag; Negative statement takes) Tj
T*
(a Positive tag.) Tj
T*
(2. Auxiliary Matching: The tag uses the identical auxiliary/modal verb from the main) Tj
T*
(statement. If no auxiliary exists, use appropriate form of 'do' \(do, does, did\).) Tj
T*
(3. Pronoun Rule: Tag subject must always be a personal pronoun matching the statement) Tj
T*
(subject.) Tj
T*
(4. Special Forms: "I am right, AREN'T I?" \(Never *amn't I\). "Let's begin, SHALL WE?".) Tj
T*
(Imperatives take "WILL YOU?" or "WON'T YOU?".) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([EXERCISE 1: Structural Classification of Sentences]) Tj
T*
(Problem: Classify each of the following sentences into Simple, Compound, Complex, or) Tj
T*
(Compound-Complex, identifying all clauses.) Tj
T*
(Sentence 1: "The bioreactor maintains sterile conditions through automated filtration.") Tj
T*
(- Classification: SIMPLE SENTENCE. \(Single independent clause; subject: The) Tj
T*
(bioreactor; verb: maintains\).) Tj
T*
(Sentence 2: "The bacterial culture grew rapidly during the logarithmic phase, and the) Tj
T*
(glucose concentration decreased steadily.") Tj
T*
(- Classification: COMPOUND SENTENCE. \(Two independent clauses joined by) Tj
T*
(coordinating conjunction ', and'\).) Tj
T*
(Sentence 3: "Because the pH dropped below 5.5, the recombinant protein precipitated out) Tj
T*
(of the aqueous buffer.") Tj
T*
(- Classification: COMPLEX SENTENCE. \(Dependent clause 'Because the pH dropped) Tj
T*
(below 5.5' + Independent clause 'the recombinant protein precipitated...'\).) Tj
T*
(Sentence 4: "When the autoclave reached 121 deg C, the timer commenced, and the) Tj
T*
(sterilization cycle ran uninterrupted for twenty minutes.") Tj
T*
(- Classification: COMPOUND-COMPLEX SENTENCE. \(Dependent clause 'When the autoclave) Tj
T*
(reached 121 deg C' + Two independent clauses linked by ', and'\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
