([EXERCISE 2: Subject-Verb Agreement \(Concord\) Mastery Drill]) Tj
T*
(Problem: Choose the grammatically correct verb in each of the following technical) Tj
T*
(statements:) Tj
T*
(Sentence 1: "A cluster of malignant tumor cells \(has / have\) been identified in the) Tj
T*
(biopsy specimen.") Tj
T*
(- Correct Verb: HAS. \(Head noun is singular 'cluster'; 'of malignant tumor cells') Tj
T*
(is an intervening prepositional phrase\).) Tj
T*
(Sentence 2: "Neither the high pressure nor the elevated temperatures \(was / were\)) Tj
T*
(sufficient to degrade the PTFE gasket.") Tj
T*
(- Correct Verb: WERE. \(In 'neither...nor', verb agrees with closest subject) Tj
T*
('elevated temperatures' [plural]\).) Tj
T*
(Sentence 3: "Ten milliliters of concentrated hydrochloric acid \(was / were\) added) Tj
T*
(dropwise to the solution.") Tj
T*
(- Correct Verb: WAS. \(Quantities of measurement, volume, time, and money are) Tj
T*
(treated as singular collective units\).) Tj
T*
(Sentence 4: "The criteria for evaluating the biosafety data \(is / are\) established by) Tj
T*
(regulatory authorities.") Tj
T*
(- Correct Verb: ARE. \('Criteria' is plural; singular form is 'criterion'\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([EXERCISE 3: Comma Splice and Run-On Sentence Correction]) Tj
T*
(Problem: Identify and repair the comma splices in the following academic excerpts using) Tj
T*
(three distinct syntactic methods:) Tj
T*
(Faulty Passage: "The primary antibodies were incubated overnight, the secondary) Tj
T*
(fluorescent markers were applied the following morning.") Tj
T*
(- Repair Method 1 \(Semicolon\): "The primary antibodies were incubated overnight;) Tj
T*
(the secondary fluorescent markers were applied the following morning.") Tj
T*
(- Repair Method 2 \(Coordinating Conjunction\): "The primary antibodies were) Tj
T*
(incubated overnight, and the secondary fluorescent markers were applied the) Tj
T*
(following morning.") Tj
T*
(- Repair Method 3 \(Subordinating Conjunction\): "After the primary antibodies were) Tj
T*
(incubated overnight, the secondary fluorescent markers were applied the following) Tj
T*
(morning.") Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([EXERCISE 4: Advanced Question Tag Construction]) Tj
T*
(Problem: Supply the correct question tag for each of the following technical) Tj
T*
(communication utterances:) Tj
T*
(Sentence 1: "The technician calibrated the analytical balance before the measurement,) Tj
T*
(________________?") Tj
T*
(- Solution: DIDN'T HE? / DIDN'T SHE? / DIDN'T THEY? \(Simple past 'calibrated') Tj
T*
(requires auxiliary 'did'; positive statement takes negative tag 'didn't'\).) Tj
T*
(Sentence 2: "None of the recombinant clones exhibited resistance to ampicillin,) Tj
T*
(________________?") Tj
T*
(- Solution: DID THEY? \('None' is negative, requiring a positive tag; pronoun for) Tj
T*
(clones is 'they'\).) Tj
T*
(Sentence 3: "I am responsible for maintaining the cleanroom environmental logs,) Tj
T*
(________________?") Tj
T*
