/F2 9.5 Tf
(>> 2.4 University Review & Examination Questions) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(* Q1: State five major rules of Subject-Verb Agreement \(Concord\) with original) Tj
T*
(illustrative sentences from biotechnology.) Tj
T*
(Answer: \(1\) Intervening phrases: Verb agrees with head noun, ignoring intervening) Tj
T*
(prepositional modifiers: 'The stability of multiple cloned plasmids IS monitored) Tj
T*
(weekly.' \(2\) Compound subjects joined by 'and' take plural verbs: 'Centrifugation and) Tj
T*
(electrophoresis ARE analytical separation techniques.' \(3\) Either...or / Neither...nor) Tj
T*
(proximity rule: Verb agrees with the nearest noun: 'Neither the primer nor the) Tj
T*
(nucleotide reagents WERE contaminated.' \(4\) Indefinite pronouns \(each, every, either,) Tj
T*
(neither\) are singular: 'Each of the PCR cycles REQUIRES precise thermal regulation.' \(5\)) Tj
T*
(Measurements of quantity, volume, and time take singular verbs: 'Fifty milligrams of) Tj
T*
(lyophilized enzyme WAS dissolved in buffer.') Tj
T*
(* Q2: Explain the Comma Splice error and discuss three distinct syntactical methods) Tj
T*
(to resolve it.) Tj
T*
(Answer: A comma splice occurs when two independent clauses \(complete grammatical) Tj
T*
(sentences\) are joined together solely by a comma without an accompanying coordinating) Tj
T*
(conjunction: 'The cells reached confluence, the media was changed.' This is) Tj
T*
(ungrammatical because a comma has insufficient structural weight to link independent) Tj
T*
(sentences. Three resolution methods: \(1\) Semicolon: Replace the comma with a semicolon) Tj
T*
(when the two thoughts are closely linked logically: 'The cells reached confluence; the) Tj
T*
(media was changed.' \(2\) Coordinating Conjunction \(FANBOYS\): Insert a coordinating) Tj
T*
(conjunction after the comma: 'The cells reached confluence, so the media was changed.') Tj
T*
(\(3\) Subordinating Conjunction: Convert one independent clause into a dependent clause:) Tj
T*
('When the cells reached confluence, the media was changed.') Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
/F2 9.5 Tf
(>> 2.5 Key Takeaways and Revision Points) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(* Compound sentences join independent clauses with coordinating conjunctions; complex) Tj
T*
(sentences combine independent and dependent clauses.) Tj
T*
(* Comma splices occur when two independent clauses are linked by a comma alone; fix) Tj
T*
(with semicolon or conjunction.) Tj
T*
(* Concord requires subject-verb agreement; intervening prepositional phrases do not) Tj
T*
(alter subject number.) Tj
T*
(* Question tags reverse statement polarity and utilize matching auxiliary verbs) Tj
T*
(\(e.g., 'I am late, aren't I?'\).) Tj
T*
